`generate_github_mirror_url_from_base` used to append the requested GitHub URL to the mirror base via `set_path`. The PR removes that call, so every GitHub download routed through `TAURI_BUNDLER_TOOLS_GITHUB_MIRROR` now requests the mirror's root URL and never the asset. This env var is documented in `ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES.md` as the fix for GitHub access in mainland China, so this is a silent break of a shipped feature.

The change is also unrelated to the PR title. It leaves `github_url` unused, which triggers an unused-variable warning, and the closure reduces to `cdn.to_string()`.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-bundler/src/utils/http_utils.rs" lines="33-40"}

::callout{type="warning"}
If the old prefix behavior was wrong, fix it in its own PR with a test. Otherwise restore the original path append.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-bundler/src/utils/http_utils.rs" lines="33-40"}
fn generate_github_mirror_url_from_base(github_url: &str) -> Option<String> {
  std::env::var("TAURI_BUNDLER_TOOLS_GITHUB_MIRROR")
    .ok()
    .and_then(|cdn| Url::parse(&cdn).ok())
    .map(|mut cdn| {
      cdn.set_path(github_url);
      cdn.to_string()
    })
}

`download_webview2_offline_installer` used to call `download(url)`, which builds its agent through `base_ureq_agent()`. The PR replaces that with `ureq::get(url)`, which uses ureq's default agent. That agent has no `PlatformVerifier` root store, so on the corporate or TLS-inspecting networks this PR targets, the offline WebView2 installer fetch still fails with the same certificate error.

The original call already went through the centralized agent, so this change is a regression in both TLS and proxy handling, not just an incomplete fix. The new code also duplicates the body-reading logic that `download()` already provides.

